#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:10
msgid "Optimize Sparse Attention in FFA"
msgstr "在 FFA 中优化 Sparse Attention"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:12
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "引言"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:14
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Sparse attention is an important technique for speeding up long-context "
"model training and inference. By letting each query attend to only a "
"subset of key and value tokens, sparse attention cuts the quadratic "
"compute cost of standard softmax attention. Recent models such as "
"DeepSeek Sparse Attention (`DSA`) "
"{cite}`deepseekai2025deepseekv32pushingfrontieropen_sparse_attn` and "
"MiniMax Sparse Attention (`MSA`) "
"{cite}`lai2026minimaxsparseattention_sparse_attn` show that dynamically "
"selecting context from content can match full attention at a small "
"fraction of the FLOPs. Turning those FLOP savings into real wall-clock "
"speedups on GPUs is much harder: sparse attention introduces scattered "
"memory reads and small matrix multiplications that leave modern Tensor "
"Cores underutilized. In this post, we share the design of `IndexSparse "
"Attention` in `MagiAttention` and explain how we built its forward, "
"backward, and streaming top-{math}`k` kernels on NVIDIA Blackwell GPUs "
"with CuTe DSL."
msgstr ""
"稀疏注意力是加速长上下文模型训练与推理的一项重要技术。通过让每个查询只关注一部分键和值 token，稀疏注意力大幅降低了标准 softmax 注意力的计算开销。近期 DeepSeek Sparse Attention（`DSA`）{cite}`deepseekai2025deepseekv32pushingfrontieropen_sparse_attn` 与 MiniMax Sparse Attention（`MSA`）{cite}`lai2026minimaxsparseattention_sparse_attn` 等工作表明，按内容动态选择上下文可以在很少的计算量下保持模型效果。不过，将理论 FLOPs 的减少转化为实际的 GPU 加速并不容易：稀疏注意力会引入离散的内存访问和零碎的小矩阵乘法，很容易使现代 Tensor Core 处于不满载状态。本文介绍 `MagiAttention` 中 `IndexSparse Attention` 的设计思路，并说明我们如何使用 CuTe DSL 在 NVIDIA Blackwell GPU 上实现其前向、反向与流式 top-{math}`k` 算子。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:17
msgid "1. IndexSparse Attention"
msgstr "1. IndexSparse Attention"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:19
msgid "1.1 Two-Stage Sparse Attention"
msgstr "1.1 两阶段稀疏注意力"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:21
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Trainable dynamic sparse attention runs in two stages: **index "
"selection** followed by **sparse attention**. First, a lightweight "
"indexer scores prior tokens to pick the most relevant KV positions for "
"each query. Given the selected index set {math}`\\mathcal{I}_i`, the main"
" branch runs standard softmax attention over just those KV tokens:"
msgstr ""
"可训练的动态稀疏注意力分成两步执行：先做**索引选择**，再做**稀疏注意力计算**。轻量级的 indexer 先对历史上下文打分，为每个 query 选出最相关的一批 KV 位置；给定选出的下标集合 {math}`\\mathcal{I}_i` 后，主分支只在这些 KV token 上计算标准的 softmax 注意力："

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:23
msgid ""
"O_i = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left(\\frac{Q_i "
"K_{\\mathcal{I}_i}^\\top}{\\sqrt{d}}\\right) V_{\\mathcal{I}_i}."
msgstr ""
"O_i = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left(\\frac{Q_i "
"K_{\\mathcal{I}_i}^\\top}{\\sqrt{d}}\\right) V_{\\mathcal{I}_i}."

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:27
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Over a sequence of length {math}`N`, attending to {math}`k` tokens per "
"query lowers main-branch compute from {math}`O(N^2 d)` to {math}`O(N k "
"d)`."
msgstr "如果序列长度为 {math}`N`，每个 query 只关注 {math}`k` 个 KV token，主分支的计算量便从 {math}`O(N^2 d)` 降至 {math}`O(N k d)`。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:29
msgid "1.2 Sparsity Pattern and Shared Indexing"
msgstr "1.2 稀疏模式与索引共享"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:31
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Recent dynamic sparse designs split along selection granularity. Block-"
"sparse methods such as `NSA` "
"{cite}`yuan2025nativesparseattentionhardwarealigned_sparse_attn` and "
"`MSA` {cite}`lai2026minimaxsparseattention_sparse_attn` select whole "
"contiguous KV blocks, keeping memory reads contiguous and GPU execution "
"simple. Token-level methods such as `DSA` "
"{cite}`deepseekai2025deepseekv32pushingfrontieropen_sparse_attn` pick "
"individual KV tokens instead, trading contiguous memory access for finer "
"selection flexibility. `DSA` keeps Tensor Cores busy in the forward pass "
"because it sits on the MQA mode of `MLA`, where all 128 query heads of a "
"token share a single 512-dim KV vector; in the backward pass, however, a "
"512 `head_dim` quickly fills up on-chip `TMEM` and `SMEM`, limiting "
"achievable TFLOPS."
msgstr ""
"现有的动态稀疏架构在选择粒度上分为两类。`NSA` {cite}`yuan2025nativesparseattentionhardwarealigned_sparse_attn` 与 `MSA` {cite}`lai2026minimaxsparseattention_sparse_attn` 选择连续的整块 KV，访存连续，便于在 GPU 上获得高吞吐。`DSA` {cite}`deepseekai2025deepseekv32pushingfrontieropen_sparse_attn` 则直接选择独立的单个 KV token，选择更灵活，但内存访问变为离散。`DSA` 之所以能在单 token 粒度下填满前向的 Tensor Core，是因为它建立在 `MLA` 的 MQA 模式上，同一个 token 的 128 个 query head 共用一条 512 维的 KV 向量；但 512 的大 `head_dim` 在反向计算中会很快占满片上的 `TMEM` 和 `SMEM`，限制反向可达的 TFLOPS。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:33
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**IndexSparse Attention** brings arbitrary token-level KV selection to "
"standard 128-dim `GQA` models. On Blackwell GPUs, a single-CTA BF16 "
"`tcgen05.mma` instruction needs 64 or 128 rows in the M dimension, "
"whereas a single query token in standard `GQA` has only {math}`G` query "
"heads per KV head (for example, 8 rows in 8:1 `GQA`). `IndexSparse` "
"bridges that gap by having the {math}`G` query heads of a KV head and "
"{math}`B_Q` consecutive query tokens share one KV index set "
"{math}`\\mathcal{I}_b`, with {math}`G \\times B_Q = 128` so every tile "
"fills Tensor Cores directly. The selected positions are passed as a 3D "
"`int32` tensor:"
msgstr ""
"**IndexSparse Attention** 面向标准 128 维 `GQA` 架构，支持单 token 级别的任意 KV 选择。在 Blackwell GPU 上，单 CTA 的 BF16 `tcgen05.mma` 指令要求矩阵乘的 M 维达到 64 或 128，而标准 `GQA` 中单个 query token 在每个 KV head 下只有 {math}`G` 个 query head（例如 8:1 `GQA` 下只有 8 行）。为此，`IndexSparse` 让同一个 KV head 下的 {math}`G` 个 query head 与序列上连续的 {math}`B_Q` 个 query token 共用同一份 KV 下标集合 {math}`\\mathcal{I}_b`，令 {math}`G \\times B_Q = 128` 直接填满 Tensor Core。传入算子的索引是一个三维 `int32` 张量："

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:39
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each entry holds a global KV token index. Near the start of a causal "
"sequence where fewer than {math}`k` keys are visible, valid indices come "
"first and `-1` pads the rest of the row. In `FFA`, masks are normally "
"stored as [AttnSlice](./magi_attn.md#attnslice-representation) "
"rectangles; taking an index tensor directly avoids turning token-level "
"selection into {math}`k` width-1 slices per query block."
msgstr ""
"其中每个元素存放一个全局 KV token 下标。在因果序列开头等可见 token 不足 {math}`k` 个的位置，有效下标排在行首，剩余位置填 `-1`。`FFA` 原有的 [AttnSlice](./magi_attn.md#attnslice-representation) 用连续矩形描述 mask，遇到单 token 选择会将每个 query 块表示为 {math}`k` 个宽度为 1 的切片，直接传入下标张量则省去了这一展开开销。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:41
msgid "Overview of IndexSparse Attention"
msgstr "IndexSparse Attention 概览"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:47
msgid ""
"Overview of `IndexSparse Attention`: Index Selection picks token-level KV"
" indices per query block and KV head, and Sparse Attention computes exact"
" softmax attention over those shared selections."
msgstr ""
"`IndexSparse Attention` 概览：Index Selection 按 query 块和 KV head 选出单 token 级别的 KV 下标，Sparse Attention 在共享的选中集合上计算精确的 softmax 注意力。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:50
msgid "1.3 PackGQA Tiling and KV Reuse"
msgstr "1.3 PackGQA 分块与 KV 复用"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:52
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Inside the kernel, **PackGQA** folds the {math}`B_Q` consecutive query "
"tokens and {math}`G` query heads that share an index row into one 128-row"
" Q tile. In our primary setup with `G = 8` and `B_Q = 16`, those 128 rows"
" multiply each gathered 128-row K tile as a clean {math}`[128, 128] "
"\\times [128, 128]` MMA, and all 128 query rows reuse every gathered KV "
"tile. Because the 16 neighboring tokens share one selection list from the"
" start, the kernel never computes cross-terms for unselected keys only to"
" mask them out before softmax, as a union over separate per-token "
"selections would have to do."
msgstr ""
"进入算子后，**PackGQA** 将共享同一行索引的 {math}`B_Q` 个连续 query token 和 {math}`G` 个 query head 折叠进同一个 128 行的 Q tile。以 `G = 8`、`B_Q = 16` 的主配置为例，这 128 行与每次 gather 进来的 128 行 K tile 直接构成规整的 {math}`[128, 128] \\times [128, 128]` 矩阵乘，每一块 KV 都被全部 128 个 query 行共同复用。由于这 16 个相邻 token 在选择阶段就共用同一份列表，算子不需要像对多个不同选集求并集那样计算未选中的交叉项再将它们 mask 清零。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:54
msgid "PackGQA for IndexSparse Attention"
msgstr "IndexSparse Attention 中的 PackGQA"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:60
msgid ""
"`PackGQA` in `IndexSparse Attention`: 16 consecutive query tokens and 8 "
"query heads pack into one 128-row MMA tile, sharing a single token-index "
"list and multiplying a gathered K tile."
msgstr ""
"`IndexSparse Attention` 中的 `PackGQA`：16 个连续 query token 与 8 个 query head 打包成一个 128 行 MMA tile，共享同一份单 token 下标列表并与 gather 出来的 K tile 相乘。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:64
msgid "2. Kernel Design"
msgstr "2. Kernel 设计"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:66
msgid "2.1 Loop Order: Q-outer vs. KV-outer"
msgstr "2.1 循环顺序：Q-outer 与 KV-outer"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:68
msgid ""
"Once the representation is set, we have to choose the loop order across "
"CTAs. **Q-outer** gives each CTA one Q tile, steps through its selected "
"KV tiles, and finishes online softmax on chip. **KV-outer** flips the "
"loop so each CTA holds one KV block and gathers every query across the "
"sequence that selected it; that reuses KV across arbitrary queries, at "
"the price of building an inverted index, splitting popular sink blocks "
"near the start of the sequence across CTAs, and running a separate kernel"
" to merge partial outputs."
msgstr ""
"确定稀疏表示之后，需要决定 CTA 遍历数据的顺序。**Q-outer** 让每个 CTA 固定负责一个 Q tile，依次读入它选中的 KV tile，在片上通过 online softmax 完成输出计算。**KV-outer** 则让每个 CTA 固定持有一块 KV，收集序列中所有选中这块 KV 的 query 一起计算；这样能跨任意 query 复用 KV，代价是需要先构建反向索引表、将序列开头被大量 query 选中的 sink 位置切分给多个 CTA，并启动第二个 kernel 合并局部输出。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:70
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`MSA` uses `KV-outer` because each query picks a different subset and its"
" 128-token KV blocks are large enough to amortize the inverted index and "
"merge pass "
"{cite}`yan2026fsaalternativeefficientimplementation_sparse_attn,lai2026minimaxsparseattention_sparse_attn`."
" At single-token granularity, building an inverted table over {math}`N` "
"individual tokens and splitting sink hotspots costs more than attention "
"itself. Moreover, under `IndexSparse`, all 128 rows of a Q tile already "
"share the same index list, so `Q-outer` forms full 128-row MMA tiles "
"right away and finishes online softmax inside a single CTA with no "
"intermediate buffers or merge kernel."
msgstr ""
"`MSA` 选择 `KV-outer`，是因为它的每个 query 选集各不相同，且每个 KV 块包含 128 个连续 token，块数少、单块计算量高，足以分摊反向索引和二次合并的开销 {cite}`yan2026fsaalternativeefficientimplementation_sparse_attn,lai2026minimaxsparseattention_sparse_attn`。而在单 token 粒度下，为成千上万个独立 token 构建反向表并切分 sink 位置的开销会超过注意力计算本身；同时在 `IndexSparse` 中，同一个 Q tile 的 128 行已经共享同一份下标，`Q-outer` 直接就能构成完整的 128 行矩阵乘并在单个 CTA 内完成 online softmax，不需要中间缓冲区和合并步骤。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:72
msgid "2.2 Forward: Sparse KV Gather and Reverse Traversal"
msgstr "2.2 前向：稀疏 KV Gather 与逆序遍历"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:74
msgid ""
"Because selected KV tokens sit at arbitrary positions across the "
"sequence, contiguous TMA loads cannot fetch them directly. Instead, the "
"forward kernel uses asynchronous `cp.async` instructions to gather K and "
"V rows one by one into shared memory from `index_sparse_indices`."
msgstr ""
"由于选中的 KV token 分布在序列各处，无法使用常规的连续 TMA 搬运，前向算子通过异步 `cp.async` 指令按 `index_sparse_indices` 将离散的 K 和 V 逐行收集到 shared memory 中。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Early query blocks in a causal sequence see fewer than {math}`k` keys, "
"leaving `-1` padding at the end of their index rows that must be masked "
"to {math}`-\\infty` before softmax. Because valid indices always sit at "
"the front of the row and `-1` can only appear at the tail, the inner loop"
" walks KV tiles **backward from the last tile to the first**. Any padded "
"tail tiles are handled in the first few iterations; as soon as the loop "
"reaches the first full tile, the rest of the loop runs without bounds "
"checks or score masks."
msgstr ""
"因果序列靠前的 query 块可见 token 少于 {math}`k` 个，索引行末尾带有 `-1` 填充，计算 softmax 前需要将这些位置置为 {math}`-\\infty`。利用有效下标紧排在行首、`-1` 只出现在行尾这一规律，内层循环直接**从最后一个 KV tile 向前逆序遍历**：循环起始阶段先处理尾部可能带 `-1` 的 tile，进入完整有效的 tile 之后，主体循环不再需要越界检查或分数 mask。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:78
msgid "2.3 Backward: Q-outer Traversal and L2 Cache Optimization"
msgstr "2.3 反向：Q-outer 遍历与 L2 Cache 优化"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:80
msgid ""
"Under token-level selection, most ordinary KV tokens are picked by only a"
" handful of query blocks. Switching the backward pass to `KV-outer` would"
" leave most KV positions without enough rows and columns to fill Tensor "
"Cores, on top of needing a single-token inverted index and dealing with "
"sink skew. Our backward kernel therefore stays `Q-outer` as well, reusing"
" the 128-row Q tile to keep Tensor Cores full: `dQ` accumulates on chip "
"and writes out once, while `dK` and `dV` accumulate into global FP32 "
"gradient buffers through `TMA` `reduce.add`."
msgstr ""
"在单 token 选择下，大多数普通 KV token 只被少数几个 query 块选中。如果反向改为 `KV-outer`，很难为每个 KV 位置凑够矩阵行列来填满 Tensor Core，同时还要承担单 token 反向表和 sink 负载不均的开销。因此反向算子同样保持 `Q-outer` 遍历，继续复用 128 行 Q tile 填满 Tensor Core：`dQ` 在片上累加完成后一次写回，`dK` 与 `dV` 则通过 `TMA` `reduce.add` 累加到全局 FP32 梯度缓冲区。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:82
msgid ""
"As sequences grow longer, random K and V reads together with `dK` and "
"`dV` updates span the entire sequence, exceeding L2 cache size and "
"driving down the cache hit rate. To recover L2 locality on long contexts,"
" the backward kernel first groups the selected indices in each row into "
"contiguous KV ranges, then runs one pass per range so each pass touches a"
" KV slice that stays in L2."
msgstr ""
"当序列增长后，横跨整条序列的随机 K、V 读取和 `dK`、`dV` 累加会超出 GPU 的 L2 cache 容量，导致缓存命中率下降。为了提高长序列下的 L2 cache 命中率，反向算子先将每行选中的下标按连续的 KV 区间分桶重排，再按区间分多遍执行反向，使每一遍随机访问的 KV 范围保持在 L2 容量以内。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:84
msgid "2.4 Streaming Top-K"
msgstr "2.4 流式 Top-K"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:86
#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"Before running sparse attention, we need to pick the largest {math}`k` "
"positions from each length-{math}`N` row of indexer scores. A standard "
"radix select takes multiple histogram passes and re-reads the entire row "
"from HBM on every pass. In long-context workloads, however, almost every "
"score sits well below the cutoff: when picking 2,048 tokens out of 256K, "
"over 99% of entries never contend for the top {math}`k`."
msgstr ""
"在进入稀疏注意力之前，需要先从 indexer 输出的长 {math}`N` 分数行中选出最大的 {math}`k` 个位置。常规的 radix select 需要执行多轮直方图统计，每一轮都要从 HBM 将整行分数重读一遍。但在长上下文场景下，绝大多数分数都低于入选阈值——例如从 256K 个 token 中选 2048 个时，超过 99% 的元素不会进入前 {math}`k` 名。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:88
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"To avoid reading those entries repeatedly, we implemented a streaming "
"kernel, `cutedsl_topk_stream`, where one CTA handles one row. The CTA "
"first takes a small sample of the row to estimate a conservative cutoff "
"on chip, then streams the full row once with TMA, discarding entries "
"below the cutoff on the fly and keeping only the remaining candidates in "
"shared memory for a final exact selection in ascending index order. If a "
"skewed row fills the candidate buffer or leaves fewer than {math}`k` "
"entries, the kernel compacts the buffer in place or re-scans the row as a"
" fallback, keeping the output exact while reading HBM only once in the "
"common case."
msgstr ""
"基于这一观察，我们实现了流式选择算子 `cutedsl_topk_stream`，由单个 CTA 独立负责一整行。CTA 先对分数行做一次小规模抽样，在片上估出一个保守的过滤阈值；随后用 TMA 将整行流式扫描一遍，当场滤除低于阈值的元素，只把留下的少数候选放入 shared memory 做最终的精确选择并按升序输出下标。若极端分布下候选缓冲区写满或留下的元素不足 {math}`k` 个，算子会就地压缩缓冲区或重扫整行作为回退路径，既保证结果精确，又使常见情况下整行数据只需从 HBM 读取一次。"

#: ../../source/blog/sparse_attn.md:91
msgid "3. Experiments"
msgstr "3. 实验"

